# Day 17/50 — Computer Networks

A computer on its own can process information.

But what happens when multiple computers need to communicate, exchange files, or share resources?
That's where computer networks come in.

A network connects two or more devices so they can communicate and share information.

From sending a simple message to accessing websites across the world, networks make it possible

And when you think about it, connection changes what something can do.

A single device has its own capabilities
But when devices work together, possibilities expand.

**Sometimes, the real power isn't in what something can do alone, but in what it can do when connected.**
